# Engineering Escalation

[Back to case overview](README.md)

Fictional educational scenario using synthetic information.

## Subject

Hydraulic cylinder stalls under load following maintenance —
cause unconfirmed

## Case Status

Open — additional technical evidence required.

## Reported Condition

The cylinder moves unloaded but slows and stops under the
usual operating load.

The motor reportedly continues running.

## Evidence Available

- Customer symptom description
- Reported timing relative to maintenance
- Technician-reported change in pressure behavior

## Evidence Missing

- Circuit drawing
- Component specifications
- Maintenance work order
- Verified load and operating conditions
- Instrument verification
- Approved diagnostic results

## Assessment

The evidence does not currently support identifying a
specific failed component.

Possible investigation areas include load conditions,
circuit configuration, hydraulic supply, and measurement
reliability.

## Actions Not Recommended

- Speculative component replacement
- Pressure-setting adjustments
- Unapproved isolation or bypass testing

## Engineering Assistance Requested

1. Identify the applicable diagnostic procedure.
2. Confirm required measurements and authorized test points.
3. Review maintenance-related configuration questions.
4. Review findings before a component-specific recommendation.

## Closure Requirements

Document the supported cause, authorized corrective action,
verification results, and customer confirmation.
